<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Glade Trail</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:127-2: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.331129" lon="-121.711243"><ele>1813.1</ele><name>Timberline Lodge</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:timberline-lodge (OSM way 149173768); confidence: high; pdf_page: 127; book_elev_ft: 5950; quote: ski west of the lodge under the Magic Mile chairlift, then west 200 yards to a wide slope, the top of the Glade Trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.332508" lon="-121.714013"><ele>1837.3</ele><name>Top of the Glade Trail</name><desc>source: upper end of OSM piste way 48946322 'Glade' (downhill run on the tram swath); the summer path Glade Trail #661 starts 100 m south; confidence: high; pdf_page: 127; quote: then west 200 yards to a wide slope, the top of the Glade Trail and also a downhill ski run</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.308538" lon="-121.752912"><ele>1222.8</ele><name>Glade Trail at Government Camp</name><desc>source: lower end of OSM piste way 1378207220 'Glade Trail' and path Glade Trail #661 (node 37724552), on Blossom Trail (street) at the top of Government Camp; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 130; quote: The trail leaves the tramway swath to enter forest on the right, following a narrower trail to Govie</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.304033" lon="-121.755862"><ele>1181.3</ele><name>Government Camp Loop at Multorpor Drive</name><desc>source: OSM node 37405606, junction of East Government Camp Loop (main street) and East Multorpor Drive/East Blossom Trail; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 130; quote: where it comes out onto the main street opposite the road to Multorpor Ski Area Sno-Park</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Glade Trail</name><desc>1. Timberline Lodge -&gt; Top of the Glade Trail: straight (high), 0.16 mi | 2. Top of the Glade Trail -&gt; Glade Trail at Government Camp: line (high), 2.70 mi | 3. Glade Trail at Government Camp -&gt; Government Camp Loop at Multorpor Drive: osm (medium), 0.38 mi</desc>
